# span: reads three characters, prints the largest code point and its negation
#
#     $ printf 'abc' | vonal run examples/span.vsr
#     99 -99
#
# A showcase, and openly so: it exists to exercise the five instructions no
# other plate needed -- IN_CHAR, ROLL, GT, POP and NEG. It still computes
# something definite, and the tests pin it across several inputs.
#
# ROLL is what makes three inputs worth having. With [a, b, c] on the stack,
# push 3 then ROLL rotates the top three so c drops to the bottom, leaving a
# and b on top to be compared without losing c. GT compares, POP discards each
# loser, NEG produces the second output.
#
# The new trick is a branch that MERGES rather than exits. Every earlier plate
# turned south only to halt. Here each GT sends the winning case south at
# columns 8 and 15; the detour discards one value and turns north to rejoin the
# main line past the SWAP POP the other case needed.
#
# The rejoin needs its own cell, which is worth knowing if you write one of
# these: a turn-north leaves the heading NORTH, so without a turn-east waiting
# at the rejoin the eye sails straight up through row 0 and loops forever. The
# first draft of this plate did exactly that and hung. Columns 11 and 18 are
# those turn-easts -- no-ops for the fall-through, heading resets for the
# detour, and the only way this language can say "carry on".
#
# The program is row 0 running straight east from (0,0), so it needs no seed
# row and no entry turn. Rows 1 to 3 hold the detours and a horizontal swell.
%plate 30x4

+3.7  +3.7  +3.7  o.37  %4.7  %3.7  %3.7  D..7  v1.7  %2.7  %1.7  >..7  %3.7  %3.7  D..7  v1.7  %2.7  %1.7  >..7  %..7  +..7  o.47  o1.7  +1.7  #5.7  +..7  o.17  o127  +1.7  ...7
o..7  o..7  o.17  o.17  o.27  o.27  o.37  o.37  >..7  %1.7  >..7  ^..7  o.67  o.67  o.77  >..7  %1.7  >..7  ^..7  o.57  o.47  o.47  o.37  o.37  o.27  o.27  o.17  o.17  o..7  o..7
o..7  o..7  o.17  o.17  o.27  o.27  o.37  o.37  o.47  o.47  o.57  o.57  o.67  o.67  o.77  o.77  o.67  o.67  o.57  o.57  o.47  o.47  o.37  o.37  o.27  o.27  o.17  o.17  o..7  o..7
o..7  o..7  o.17  o.17  o.27  o.27  o.37  o.37  o.47  o.47  o.57  o.57  o.67  o.67  o.77  o.77  o.67  o.67  o.57  o.57  o.47  o.47  o.37  o.37  o.27  o.27  o.17  o.17  o..7  o..7
